   "input": "/bin/zsh -c 'cat /var/folders/3g/vf36b0b14wzd0fgsgtdp06h00000gp/T/writing-probe/p-3f25f938/81bbef76.txt'",
   "output": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# sackview: see inside a ZIP before you unpack it\n\nList archive entries and check their sizes before extracting elsewhere.\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\nZIP archives only \u00b7 Offline inspection\n\n## Archive inspection\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\nEach entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Commands\n\n### Find the largest entries\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\nShow the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first.\n\n### Filter by name\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\nShow only entries whose names match the pattern.\n\n## Keys\n\nNo key bindings are specified in the supplied reference.\n\n## Check disk space before extracting\n\nsackview displays the total unpacked size. Use it to check available disk space before extracting the archive elsewhere.\n\n## Good to know\n\n**Archive safety**  \nsackview never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n\n**Privacy**  \nNo archive contents are sent to a service.\n\n**Unsupported formats**  \nOther archive formats produce an unsupported-format message and return exit code 24.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) What does sackview show you?\n(b) What command lists the entries in photos.zip?\n(c) Does sackview extract files?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (c) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
